---
import Prose from '../components/Prose.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';
import { PRODUCTS, GUIDES, COMPARES } from '../lib/data';
---
<Prose title="About Enthusiast Review: Who We Are and How We Pick" h1="About Enthusiast Review" description="Who runs Enthusiast Review, how we pick PC parts from spec sheets, platform requirements and independent measurements, and how the site makes money." dek="PC hardware buying guides since 2019, built around the question every builder asks: will this part suit my build?">
  <p>{SITE.name} is an independent buying-guide site for PC hardware. We started in {SITE.founded} with guides to CPU coolers, power supplies, graphics cards and cases for the Ryzen 3000 generation, and we now track {PRODUCTS.length} parts across eight categories, with {GUIDES.length} best lists and {COMPARES.length} head-to-head comparisons.</p>
  <h2>What we do differently</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>We check the platform, not just the part.</strong> A graphics card with eight PCIe lanes behaves differently in an old PCIe 3.0 board. A Ryzen 9000 chip needs a BIOS update on early B650 boards. A 168 mm cooler will not fit a 160 mm case. We say so before you buy.</li>
    <li><strong>We use the broad pattern, not one chart.</strong> Performance claims on this site reflect what the wider independent hardware press has published, rounded to what holds across many games and reviews.</li>
    <li><strong>We say what we don't know.</strong> We do not run a test lab. Our {SITE.score} is a research score, and every page says so.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>How we make money</h2>
  <p>When you buy through links on our pages we may earn an affiliate commission, mostly from Amazon. That never changes which product we pick or how we rank it. Read our full <a href="/disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a> and <a href="/how-we-review/">how we score</a>.</p>
  <h2>Get in touch</h2>
  <p>Spotted a wrong spec, a discontinued part or a BIOS gotcha we missed? Email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>. Corrections are our favorite kind of mail.</p>
</Prose>
